{"op": "append", "content": "[\ud83d\udc1e] [2026-02-01 23:48:57 UTC] [Agent: Orchestrator] [Project: query_enhancement_suite] [BUG] open_bug template population incomplete - agents skip follow-up edits: open_bug creates a bug report with partial template population. Only Bug Overview fields (ID, reporter, date, severity, status) and symptoms text get filled. Remaining sections (Description/Expected Behaviour, Steps to Reproduce, Investigation/Root Cause, Resolution Plan, Timeline, Appendix) stay as raw placeholder text like [What should happen]. Agents are told to follow up with manage_docs replace_section calls but consistently skip this step, leaving incomplete bug reports. The workflow is two-step (open_bug then manual section edits) but should either: (a) accept more content upfront to populate more sections, or (b) enforce completion before the bug is considered filed. | affected_paths=[\"tools/sentinel.py\", \"tools/manage_docs.py\", \"utils/templates/\"]; case_type=bug; landing_status=proposed; symptoms=open_bug creates a bug report with partial template population. Only Bug Overview fields (ID, reporter, date, severity, status) and symptoms text get filled. Remaining sections (Description/Expected Behaviour, Steps to Reproduce, Investigation/Root Cause, Resolution Plan, Timeline, Appendix) stay as raw placeholder text like [What should happen]. Agents are told to follow up with manage_docs replace_section calls but consistently skip this step, leaving incomplete bug reports. The workflow is...; title=open_bug template population incomplete - agents skip follow-up edits; priority=high; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/query_enhancement_suite/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-01T23:48:57.144051+00:00_d31e243f", "timestamp": "2026-02-01T23:48:57.144124+00:00"}
