{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-02-01 23:52:00 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-CouncilSessions] [Project: query_enhancement_suite] CRITICAL GAP IDENTIFIED: Scribe's scribe_entries table lacks session_id column. Council_MCP's god_memories and god_audit_entries both have session_id FK linking to god_sessions table. This is the fundamental architectural difference preventing session-based querying in Scribe. Without session_id on entries, cannot filter query_entries by session. | confidence=1; council_pattern=session_id_on_all_records; critical_finding=missing_session_fk; impact=cannot_filter_by_session; reasoning={\"how\": \"Compared Council's god_memories schema (line 529: session_id field) with Scribe's scribe_entries schema (line 854-867: no session_id field)\", \"what\": \"Council stores session_id on every memory and audit entry, Scribe only tracks sessions separately without linking to entries\", \"why\": \"This gap explains why query_entries cannot filter by session - the data model doesn't support it\"}; scribe_gap=no_session_tracking_in_entries; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/query_enhancement_suite/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-01T23:52:00.860160+00:00_463664df", "timestamp": "2026-02-01T23:52:00.860235+00:00"}
