{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-02-02 02:14:43 UTC] [Agent: Orchestrator] [Project: query_enhancement_suite] Fixed MCP stdout pollution that breaks Claude.ai JSON-RPC client: (1) Redirected all print() calls in utils/reminder_validator.py to stderr (added import sys, added file=sys.stderr to 15 print calls). (2) Added HF_HUB_DISABLE_PROGRESS_BARS=1 env var in plugins/vector_indexer.py to suppress HuggingFace model loading progress bars. (3) Redirected all 32 bare print() calls in server.py to stderr. | files_changed=[\"utils/reminder_validator.py\", \"plugins/vector_indexer.py\", \"server.py\"]; how=Redirected all print() to stderr, set HF_HUB_DISABLE_PROGRESS_BARS env var; what=print() calls and HF progress bars were going to stdout during server init; why=MCP protocol requires only JSON-RPC on stdout; any other output causes Claude.ai client to fail JSON.parse; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/query_enhancement_suite/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-02T02:14:43.867715+00:00_79efdef8", "timestamp": "2026-02-02T02:14:43.867756+00:00"}
