{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-02-02 04:00:01 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-QueryEntries] [Project: query_enhancement_suite] CRITICAL FINDING: query_entries reads flat PROGRESS_LOG.md files (line 647: read_all_lines(log_path)) and parses each line with parse_log_line() (line 667). This is completely different from read_recent which uses storage_backend.fetch_recent_entries() to query the DB directly. | confidence=1; files_touched=[\"tools/query_entries.py\"]; lines=[647, 667]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Direct code inspection of tools/query_entries.py lines 590-750, identified read_all_lines() and parse_log_line() as flat-file parsing mechanism\", \"what\": \"Two completely different execution paths: query_entries (file \\u2192 parse \\u2192 filter) vs read_recent (DB \\u2192 format)\", \"why\": \"Understanding data flow divergence - query_entries uses flat file parsing while read_recent uses DB\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/query_enhancement_suite/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-02T04:00:01.479326+00:00_a82f6542", "timestamp": "2026-02-02T04:00:01.479366+00:00"}
