{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-02-02 04:05:07 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-QueryEntries] [Project: query_enhancement_suite] RESEARCH COMPLETE: Investigated query_entries flat-file vs DB inconsistency. ROOT CAUSE: _is_template_entry() in utils/logs.py filters ALL entries containing \"template\" keyword (line 20), treating legitimate log entries as placeholders. ARCHITECTURAL DIVERGENCE: query_entries uses flat file parsing, read_recent uses DB directly. UNUSED INFRASTRUCTURE: storage backend has functional query_entries() methods (sqlite.py:594-673) that are never called. CROSS-PROJECT SEARCH: Works but inherits same parsing bug. MIGRATION PATH: Trivial (~10 lines) to switch to DB. See RESEARCH_QUERY_ENTRIES_FLATFILE_DB_20260202.md for full analysis. | confidence=1; doc_out=RESEARCH_QUERY_ENTRIES_FLATFILE_DB_20260202.md; entry_type=research_complete; files_analyzed=[\"tools/query_entries.py\", \"tools/read_recent.py\", \"utils/logs.py\", \"storage/base.py\", \"storage/sqlite.py\"]; findings_count=6; reasoning={\"how\": \"Systematic code tracing, data flow comparison, storage backend analysis, log file verification\", \"what\": \"Root cause identified, architectural divergence documented, migration path clear, cross-project search analyzed\", \"why\": \"Research phase complete - all questions answered with evidence\"}; stage=research; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/query_enhancement_suite/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-02T04:05:07.764526+00:00_6d437fd8", "timestamp": "2026-02-02T04:05:07.764593+00:00"}
