{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-02-02 04:06:59 UTC] [Agent: ArchitectAgent-SearchQueryFix] [Project: query_enhancement_suite] Research documents reviewed. Verified key findings: (1) scribe.search has no pagination, unbounded line length in Match objects, no output size limits - causes 794K char responses; (2) query_entries uses flat file parsing with _is_template_entry() filter that silently drops entries containing \"template\" keyword, while read_recent uses DB correctly. Now verifying code reality. | issues_identified=[\"scribe.search output explosion\", \"query_entries template filtering bug\", \"query_entries flat file vs DB divergence\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Use scribe.read_file to inspect key files mentioned in research\", \"what\": \"Verify Match object structure, search loop limits, _is_template_entry() logic, storage backend methods\", \"why\": \"Ground architecture in verified code reality before designing fixes\"}; research_docs_read=2; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/query_enhancement_suite/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-02-02T04:06:59.654207+00:00_bce48a95", "timestamp": "2026-02-02T04:06:59.654250+00:00"}
